WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:05.890
With his strategic moves and secretive whispers,
Otto Hightower is definitely reminding some

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.910
"House of the Dragon" fans of some of the
shrewdest players on "Game of Thrones."

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.390
Throughout the first four episodes of "House
of the Dragon," which serves as both a spin-off

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.750
of and a prequel to the HBO juggernaut "Game
of Thrones," plenty of characters are vying

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.610
for the Iron Throne, including Otto Hightower.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:26.340
As Hand of the King to Viserys I as well as
two other kings before him, Otto knows what

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.340
it's like to be in close proximity to ultimate
power.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.000
Much like Tywin Lannister from the original
"Game of Thrones," Otto is a quiet yet skilled

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.130
schemer, frequently holding his tongue until
the right moment where he can play his cards

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.130
accordingly.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:44.060
By Episode 4, this tactic has succeeded nicely
for him, as his daughter Alicent Hightower

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.290
is now married to Viserys and has had two
children — one of which is a boy.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.730
"Hail, hail!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:55.470
Aegon the conqueror babe, second of his name!"

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.270
In the fourth episode of "House of the Dragon,"
"King of the Narrow Sea," Otto doesn't do

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:04.130
a whole lot, but he does make one crucial
move just before it draws to a close.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:08.240
After Princess Rhaenyra and Prince Daemon
Targaryen give into their desire for one another

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:12.600
in a brothel in King's Landing, a confidante
referred to as the "White Worm" tells Otto

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.250
that the uncle and niece were spotted together.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.750
Otto quickly takes this information to Viserys.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.080
The king dismisses this information as nothing
more than a transparent ploy to get Alicent's

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.790
son Aegon onto the throne instead of Rhaenyra.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.610
That said, Viserys later makes it clear to
Rhaenyra that he does possibly believe Otto.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:32.560
"The truth does not matter, Rhaenyra!

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:34.729
Only perception!"

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:39.130
Even with Viserys' potential belief that Otto's
information was true, Otto is essentially

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:40.910
fired as Hand of the King.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.240
But he still has plenty of cards up his sleeve.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.960
His daughter Alicent is still the beloved
second queen to Viserys, and at the rate she's

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.420
going, she might end up giving birth to another
heir before long.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.490
Plus, Aegon is certainly a viable candidate
for King.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:57.970
Also, Otto may well have a stronger influence
the further he gets from the throne, working

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.020
from the shadows to achieve his goals.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:04.280
The show has frequently alluded to the fact
that he has collaborators lurking in Oldtown;

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.390
maybe we'll finally get to see what alliances
he's formed there.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.159
Throughout the series thus far, Otto has shown
himself to be shrewd to, perhaps, a fault.

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:16.569
In the aftermath of Viserys' wife's death,
he wastes little to no time in sending Alicent

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:21.159
to "comfort" the king, resulting in a betrothal
between the teenage girl and much older, physically

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:22.459
ailing Viserys.

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:26.760
He also even suggests to Viserys that Rhaenyra
— for whom Viserys is desperately trying

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.069
to find a suitable husband — marry her younger
half-brother Aegon, who is, at that point,

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:32.189
two years old.

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:36.639
Viserys might have fallen for Alicent's nightly
visits, but even he's disgusted by Otto's

00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:39.849
proposition to marry Rhaenyra and Aegon.

00:02:39.849 --> 00:02:43.920
All in all, Otto's tactics are likely to remind
fans of Petyr "Littlefinger" Baelish as well

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.459
as Tywin Lannister.

00:02:45.459 --> 00:02:47.959
He's also definitely grossing audiences out.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:52.090
What he does next remains to be seen, but
now that he's no longer Hand, he may have

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:55.379
to return to Oldtown to rally the troops he
apparently has there.

00:02:55.379 --> 00:02:58.349
So we may get to revisit that location before
long.

